Return early from initialize_screen() with no video info

kernel_bootstrap_thread() calls initialize_screen(NULL, kPEAcquireScreen).  With
a NULL boot_vinfo the setup block that maps the framebuffer and assigns gc_ops is
skipped, so the kPEAcquireScreen branch runs vc_progress_set() and gc_enable()
with gc_ops still at its defaults.

That call is where run-253 stops: Q2 prints and Q3 never does, with nothing else
between them.  run-253 also carried a guard on vinfo.v_depth == 0, which did not
fire, so the depth is non-zero and the branch was taken.

Nothing in this function can work without boot_vinfo, and this port's console is
the injected blob, so return immediately.  The call site stays, so the symbol
stays referenced (dropping it broke the bsd link in run-254).
---
diff --git a/osfmk/console/video_console.c b/osfmk/console/video_console.c
index 384118e..9fcc340 100644
--- a/osfmk/console/video_console.c
+++ b/osfmk/console/video_console.c
@@ -2792,6 +2792,23 @@ void
 initialize_screen(PE_Video * boot_vinfo, unsigned int op)
 {
 	unsigned int newMapSize = 0;
+
+	/*
+	 * nio: called once from kernel_bootstrap_thread() with a NULL boot_vinfo.
+	 *
+	 * With no boot_vinfo the setup block below is skipped entirely: no mapping
+	 * is made, gc_ops is never assigned and gc_initialize() never runs, so vinfo
+	 * keeps whatever the console blob left there.  The kPEAcquireScreen branch
+	 * then runs vc_progress_set() and gc_enable() anyway, and that is where the
+	 * boot stops -- Q2 prints, Q3 never does, with this call as the only
+	 * statement in between.
+	 *
+	 * There is nothing to initialise without boot_vinfo, and this port's console
+	 * is the injected blob, so return before touching any of it.
+	 */
+	if (boot_vinfo == NULL) {
+		return;
+	}
 	vm_offset_t newVideoVirt = 0;
 	boolean_t graphics_now;
 	uint32_t delay;
